"01_coerce.mst — argument coercion for generated external calls (DD6c).

 HAND-WRITTEN. The generated prims take WORDS, because that is what the FFI
 floor takes. Real Dolphin code passes objects: a String where LPCWSTR is
 wanted, an ExternalMemory where a struct pointer is wanted, nil for a null
 pointer. This is the seam, and the generator emits calls into it from the type
 information in Dolphin's own pragma.

 A runtime layer rather than code inlined into 1,126 wrappers: the rules are the
 same everywhere, and one place to fix them is worth more than saving a send.
 Where a coercion allocates, the selector says so (`...Temp`) and the caller
 frees under ensure:."

Object subclass: FFICoerce [

    "A word argument: integers pass through, nil is the null pointer, booleans
     are Win32 BOOLs. Anything else is a caller bug and says so — a silent
     coercion here would put a plausible number into a real API call."
    FFICoerce class >> word: x [
        x isNil ifTrue: [ ^0 ].
        x == true ifTrue: [ ^1 ].
        x == false ifTrue: [ ^0 ].
        x isInteger ifTrue: [ ^x ].
        (x isKindOf: ExternalMemory) ifTrue: [ ^x address ].
        ^self error: 'FFI: cannot pass ', x class name, ' as a word argument'
    ]

    "A pointer argument. nil is null; ExternalMemory passes its address; an
     Integer is a raw address the caller already holds."
    FFICoerce class >> pointer: x [
        x isNil ifTrue: [ ^0 ].
        (x isKindOf: ExternalMemory) ifTrue: [ ^x address ].
        x isInteger ifTrue: [ ^x ].
        ^self error: 'FFI: cannot pass ', x class name, ' as a pointer argument'
    ]

    "An LPCWSTR argument. A String is copied into a fresh UTF-16 buffer which
     the CALLER frees — hence the name. Answers the buffer, not the address, so
     the caller can free it; the address is taken at the call site."
    FFICoerce class >> stringTemp: x [
        x isNil ifTrue: [ ^nil ].
        (x isKindOf: ExternalMemory) ifTrue: [ ^x ].
        x isString ifTrue: [ ^Utf16Buffer fromString: x ].
        ^self error: 'FFI: cannot pass ', x class name, ' as a string argument'
    ]

    FFICoerce class >> addressOf: x [
        x isNil ifTrue: [ ^0 ].
        ^x address
    ]
]
